@100 = ~Stolen Flute
Hiarfi, a young bard from Waterdeep, lost the ceremonial flute he received upon graduating from New Olamn. Wet bootprints led west from his room in the inn. The thief may have passed into the Bridge District or River District. Hiarfi promised 400 gold if I can recover his instrument.~
@101 = ~Stolen Flute
I recovered Hiarfi's flute and returned it to him at the inn. His treasured graduation instrument is safely in his hands again.~

// CotSC translation batch 5: dialogue text extracted; old entries preserved.
@102 = ~My flute is back where it belongs. Thanks again. I can finally return to my music.~
@103 = ~My flute! You really found it! By Chauntea's mercy, I was so afraid I'd be shamed forever. Here, take this potion and four hundred gold, as I promised. I can finally go back to work.~
@104 = ~Have you found any trace of my flute? Please don't give up. I can't imagine returning to Waterdeep without it.~
@105 = ~Not yet. I'll keep looking.~
@106 = ~Can you tell me more about the flute?~
@107 = ~Any clues?~
@108 = ~Oh, it's you again. Are you willing to help me out or not?~
@109 = ~Tell me about this flute.~
@110 = ~Is there anything else you can tell us? Any clues?~
@111 = ~I don't really have time for this right now.~
@112 = ~Won't you spare a second for a friend in need?~
@113 = ~What do you need?~
@114 = ~Do I know you?~
@115 = ~No.~
@116 = ~A favour. Judging by your appearance, your way of life may be just what I need. Whether you're thugs, soldiers, bounty hunters or travellers, I don't care. You look like hardened warriors, and I'm in dire need of such people.~
@117 = ~My name is Hiarfi, a rising bard from Waterdeep. I recently graduated from New Olamn, and I'm trying to make a name for myself. The long journey took its toll on me, but I'm sure that's only temporary. Alas, a far greater misfortune befell me when I set foot in this filthy city. My prized instrument has been stolen.~
@118 = ~I was awarded a gift: a flute. As soon as I came through the city gates and settled into this inn, I took my eyes off it for a single moment, and it was gone. Groncaner is about as useful as a wooden frying pan, and the guards are... well, guards. That flute is proof of my rank and title. My most treasured possession.~
@119 = ~Please, will you help me find the thief and bring back my flute? This is my life! Losing it is... like losing a limb.~
@120 = ~Tell me about this flute.~
@121 = ~You mentioned New Olamn. What is that?~
@122 = ~Is there anything else you can tell us? Any clues?~
@123 = ~I don't really have time for this right now.~
@124 = ~Suit yourself. I'll be here, if you change your mind or find someone else who can help.~
@125 = ~Our degrees officially recognise us across Faerûn as Master Bards. The title carries political influence, respect among high society, and access to noble courts throughout the Sword Coast. The instruments we receive are symbols of our graduation and the status we've earned.~
@126 = ~My flute is the heart of my dedication. Without it, I cannot prove my membership in the college, and I'll be the laughingstock of every bard I meet. Usually I'd call upon my professional contacts to track it down, but... I cannot do so at present.~
@127 = ~I'm not looking for pity, but for help.~
@128 = ~So, what will it be? Will you help me?~
@129 = ~You mentioned New Olamn. What is that?~
@130 = ~Is there anything else you can tell us? Any clues?~
@131 = ~I don't really have time for this right now.~
@132 = ~It's a prestigious and highly competitive magical university in Waterdeep, where I come from. A fabulous place! Any aspiring bard should consider enrolling, if they can afford it. Students undergo intensive memory training alongside musical instruction, ancient history, local politics and magical lore.~
@133 = ~Graduating with high marks earns you a special instrument, such as my flute. It represents the highest honour a bard can achieve there. I simply cannot let it be stolen. I must get it back!~
@134 = ~Tell me about this flute.~
@135 = ~Is there anything else you can tell us? Any clues?~
@136 = ~I don't really have time for this right now.~
@137 = ~Only one thing I noticed: wet bootprints leading out of my room. I tried to follow them, but they vanished outside. The thief went west. Perhaps the Bridge District or River District? That's what the people I questioned suggested, at least.~
@138 = ~I'll find it for you. At least I'll give it a try.~
@139 = ~I don't really have time for this right now.~
@140 = ~I'd appreciate it greatly if your efforts aren't in vain. I'll pay you four hundred gold coins as a reward. Do your best out there.~
@141 = ~Huh. I thought you had more common sense. Well, find me if you change your mind.~
@142 = ~An instrument to a bard is like a lifeforce. We sacrifice plenty to become what we are. My heart aches with sorrow for you, young bard.~
